            "advisory": {
              "id": "RUSTSEC-2024-0449",
              "package": "unsafe-libyaml",
              "title": "unsafe-libyaml is unmaintained",
              "description": "The [repository](https://github.com/dtolnay/unsafe-libyaml) was archived by\nits owner on 2024-03-25 and is read-only. The last release is 0.2.11\n(March 2024).\n\n`unsafe-libyaml` is a machine translation of libyaml's C code into unsafe\nRust (c2rust). Bugs found in it will not be fixed upstream. It is used by\n`serde_yaml` (itself deprecated) and by forks such as `serde_yaml_ng`.\n\n## Alternatives\n\nConsider a YAML parser written in safe Rust, for example:\n\n- [saphyr](https://crates.io/crates/saphyr) ([serde-saphyr](https://crates.io/crates/serde-saphyr) for serde users)\n- [noyalib](https://crates.io/crates/noyalib)",
